.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 10, 2026
.Dt BSDMEMORY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm BSDMemory
.Nd publish bounded memory-pressure state
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs unprivileged in capability mode and samples three BSDSysctl counters:
.Va vm.stats.vm.v_free_count ,
.Va vm.stats.vm.v_free_min ,
and
.Va vm.stats.vm.v_free_target .
Its explicit policy grants only these reads and no writes or kernel tokens.
The counters are sampled separately and are not an atomic VM snapshot.
.Pp
The latest state is published through BSDNotify at
.Va system.memory.pressure :
0 normal, 1 warning, 2 critical, or 3 unknown.
Free pages at or below the minimum threshold mean critical; pages at or
below the target mean warning.
Higher free-page counts mean normal.
Escalation is immediate; recovery requires three consecutive lower-pressure
samples.
Read failures or inconsistent thresholds publish unknown and reset recovery.
The last valid pressure restriction is retained internally; recovery after
a failure still requires three consecutive lower-pressure samples.
These are free-page watermarks, not a prediction of allocation failure or a
complete accounting of reclaimable filesystem caches.
.Pp
Sampling occurs approximately once a second, subject to bounded source RPCs.
Notification state is checked even when unchanged so router restart can be
recovered.
BSDNotify reserves this state topic for the authenticated label
.Va system.Memory/bsdmemory ,
including before the producer starts and after it disconnects.
The producer's gated notification policy permits only this topic.
No client payload can choose a publisher identity.
.Pp
Use
.Dl notifyctl state-watch system.memory.pressure 10 5000
to inspect changes.
A missing state or an unknown value must not be interpreted as normal.
A stopped producer loses ownership when its last session disconnects.
.Sh OOM PROTECTION
The shipped manifest requests
.Va oom_protect = true .
Switchboard applies the kernel's
.Dv P_PROTECTED
OOM exclusion before allowing the program to execute.
BSDNotify and BSDSysctl request the same exclusion because they are required
by this notification path; Capsule protects the supervisor at bootstrap.
Only bundles loaded from the trusted system registry may request this policy.
Failure to apply it prevents launch.
The daemon remains unprivileged and cannot grant this exemption to clients.
The exemption survives exec and credential changes, is not inherited by
forked children, and ends when the process exits.
It excludes the process from the kernel OOM victim selector; it does not
reserve RAM, prevent allocation failures, or override deliberate supervisor
shutdown, fatal faults, resource-limit enforcement or kernel panic.
Signal shields remain a separate protection.
.Sh DEPENDENCY RECOVERY
Sampling and pressure publication each use a 400 millisecond libservice RPC
budget, including discovery and handshake waits.  Failed dependencies retry
with exponential delays from one to thirty seconds.  Success resets the delay.
Health transitions and cumulative failure counts are logged once per transition.
Missing samples retain the last valid pressure restriction.
These budgets bound RPC waits, not arbitrary kernel stalls, allocation or
mutex contention.  The provider heartbeat uses a separate 400 millisecond
budget so a failed supervisor does not cause an unlimited reply wait.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr BSDNotify 8 ,
.Xr BSDSysctl 8 ,
.Xr notifyctl 8
